
# 17. Binary Search Tree (BST)

## Question Description
Implement a Binary Search Tree in C++. Insert elements into the tree and perform inorder traversal. In a BST, values smaller than a node are placed in its left subtree, and values greater than the node are placed in its right subtree.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60, 80]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`20 30 40 50 60 70 80`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[10, 5, 15]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`5 10 15`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[8, 3, 12, 1]`

Expected Output (Inorder):
`1 3 8 12`

## Time Complexity
- Average insertion: O(log n)
- Worst-case insertion: O(n)
- Inorder traversal: O(n)

## Space Complexity
- O(h) recursion stack for recursive operations, where h is the tree height.
